-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+### 2Q Replacement Policy
+
+The private cache uses 2Q replacement to separate first-use screening sheets from repeatedly accessed comparison sheets:
+
+- **Probationary queue (`A1in`)**: A FIFO queue holding newly rendered, first-use contact sheets, bounded to a configured byte share of the 12 GiB budget. One-off sequential screening scans cycle through `A1in` without displacing the protected working set.
+- **Ghost queue (`A1out`)**: A bounded FIFO queue storing only cache keys (no JPEG bytes) for sheets recently evicted from `A1in`, allowing a sheet requested again shortly after eviction to be recognized as reused.
+- **Main queue (`Am`)**: An LRU queue holding reused contact sheets, occupying the remainder of the 12 GiB budget.
+
+Admission, promotion, and eviction rules:
+
+- **First-time admission** (key not in `A1out`): Admit the completed sheet into `A1in`. Before admitting, if `A1in` plus the new sheet would exceed `A1in`'s byte share (or total cached bytes would exceed 12 GiB), evict from the tail of `A1in` and record each evicted key in `A1out` (dropping the oldest ghost key when `A1out` is at capacity). If `A1in` is empty and total bytes still exceed 12 GiB, evict from the tail of `Am`.
+- **Re-admission from ghost queue** (key present in `A1out`): Remove the key from `A1out` and admit the completed sheet into `Am`, evicting least-recently-used entries from `Am` (and then `A1in` if needed) so total cached JPEG data stays within 12 GiB.
+- **Cache hit in `Am`**: Move the entry to the most-recently-used position in `Am`.
+- **Cache hit in `A1in`**: Promote the entry from `A1in` to the most-recently-used position in `Am`, evicting from `Am` if needed to maintain queue bounds.
+
+All queue structures, ghost keys, and split parameters are private to the preview worker.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q (probationary FIFO `A1in`, ghost queue `A1out`, main LRU `Am`) | LRU; frequency-based eviction with aging | Protects repeatedly accessed comparison sheets from being flushed by long sequential screenings without the stale-popularity lag of aged frequency counters, at the cost of extra queue bookkeeping and a tunable queue-size split. All changes stay inside the preview worker's private cache. |
+
